    <h1>About</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="about-body">
    <p>I’m Neil Kodner, a photographer based in Los Gatos, California.</p>
    <p>Hockey is a major part of my photography. Away from the rink, I photograph cities and the people in them.</p>
    <p>I’m looking for editorial assignments and team or league media work, in hockey above all.</p>

    <section class="about-more" aria-labelledby="building">
      <h2 id="building">Building for photographers</h2>
      <p>I photograph hockey and other fast action, often in long bursts on a Sony Alpha 1 II, and one game leaves a couple of thousand frames to go through. I wanted a faster way to review and cull them, so I built a Mac app for my own shoots. It became Palomino.</p>
      <p>Palomino shows the preview the camera already embeds in each RAW file, so the next frame is on screen the moment I press a key. I rate and reject from the keyboard and hand the keepers to Lightroom. It doesn’t choose for me. It makes looking at every frame fast enough that I still do it myself. It runs locally on the Mac, sells for a one-time price with no subscription, and other photographers now pay for it too. It’s at <a href="https://palomino-app.com">palomino-app.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

